          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "Not until you know why it fails. Loosening it is fine only if the assert was over-specified, for example it pinned an exact float, an ordering, or a timestamp that doesn't matter. If it's catching real behavior, loosening it hides a bug.\n\nQuick check: does the actual value still meet what the code is supposed to guarantee?\n- **Yes:** the assert was wrong. Loosen it to the real contract, not just enough to pass.\n- **No:** fix the code.\n- **Flaky:** fix the nondeterminism rather than widening the tolerance.\n\nIf you paste the assert and the failure output, I can tell you which case it is."
